 teacher at  ua during his spare time  i wholeheartedly think this would be the  case and there are a few reasons here  for those of you who've seen my next  generation video you'll know that by the  time we get to 10 years in the future  it would only be right that ua has  reformed the entrance exam  to accommodate heroes who don't have  combat focused quirks for example kids  with healing powers you know they're not  going to be destroying robots exactly  but yeah kids like that in the future  will get onto the course  and so for those students they'd likely  need additional classes to help build up  their basic strength  in the absence of izawa hitoshi would be  the perfect teacher for this  the professor wouldn't be available  because by this point in the storyline  if he's alive  i reckon izawa would be headmaster at ua  he was always someone who did things in  his own unorthodox way  so putting him in charge of the school  is what i think could lead to the  wholesale changes that i spoke about in  the first next generation video  especially regarding the entrance exam  as that was one of the things that  aizawa specifically said he did not like  the other reason i think he wouldn't  teach these classes is because  i mean he might be dead by this point as  i record this video the last chapter of  my academia  was 276 where we saw deku attacking  sugaraki  um so i'm really hoping you know by the  time i put this video out  that izawa has not died but even if he  survives this whole encounter in this  current war arc  we can't act like it's a certainty that  he'll live the next 10 years  so yeah it is possible that he might  have died either way whichever one  happens  shinzo is best placed to be the  inspirational teacher  to be giving these extra classes to kids  who need to build up their physical  strength  because he was i mean he's the  embodiment of that he's someone who came  into ua  with no strength whatsoever izara even  noted during the  sports festival that even though deku  wasn't at the level of a hero core  student  he was still way physically stronger  than shinzo by agreeing to teach these  kids alongside being a hero  he would have not only fulfilled his  goal of becoming a great hero  but also being one who helps raise the  next generation of heroes exactly like  him  because this is a time skip video i  think it's only right that i also talk  about  the most likely quirk evolutions after  all this time  currently shinzo has two big limitations  the first being that his enemies can  break out of his trance with a slap to  the head  or some other kind of physical force  this is a big deal  as if he's up against villains who are  working together then brainwashing one  of them is pretty useless if the others  can easily break them out  in my opinion the way it works right now  is a bit too flimsy  so to me in the future perhaps hitoshi  could brainwash people to the extent  where they genuinely can't escape unless  shinzo himself takes physical damage  this would be reminiscent of the way  that seji's quirk works in that he can  trap people inside his meat and they  can't escape they can't do anything to  break out  but if people on the outside were to  attack the user  then yeah in that situation they can  escape the second biggest weakness  currently of this quirk  is that he can't actually make people  draw on their own knowledge when giving  commands  he can give you basic instructions for  people to do things like walk out the  ring for example  but if you brainwash the villain and ask  them to type a code to disable a bomb or  something crazy like that  they wouldn't do it because that  requires them to think it would also be  super useful to use on villains in  tartus prison  as you can get vital information out of  them remember in the manga how they  tried so hard to get kirigiri to give up  any relevant information  well in the next gen you know if there's  a villain like that they could just call  shinzo in and he could literally just  brainwash the person and make them give  up whatever information they know  if you're interested in learning about  his upgrades more in depth then be sure  to check out this video i did last year  which explains all of that thank you  guys for watching as always  i'm currently away visiting family but i  recorded this video in advance so that i  could still put something out this week  so if you enjoyed it you know then i'd  appreciate if you could hit that  subscribe button  if you haven't already peace out

